== mutant 1: FIXTURE_COMMITS dates lose their +00:00 offset ==
E       AssertionError: the fixture's HEAD depends on the building machine's timezone: TZ=Pacific/Kiritimati gave 36737888c75fb6e10d092b7421f82c3194f817f4, TZ=America/Los_Angeles gave 043b58a628b36aa1df0e390759a459bdb77edbdc. Every date in conftest.FIXTURE_COMMITS must carry an explicit offset — the control above measured '2026-08-27 16:49:56 +1400' against '2026-08-27 16:49:56 -0700' for one bare string. Without it, AC-040's deterministic hashes across machines is false and every drift assertion naming a commit becomes a local result.
1 failed, 4 deselected in 0.65s
== mutant 2: build_fixture_repo stops passing env to git ==
E       AssertionError: the control did not diverge: the fixture built with every date overridden to '2026-08-27T16:49:56', which carries no offset, reached the same HEAD (d30d7d33a0bd3b878985789bdfd132034cb5b4b9) under TZ=Pacific/Kiritimati and TZ=America/Los_Angeles. Either build_repo's env is not reaching the git child — in which case the assertion below compares two builds in one timezone and can only pass — or this machine has no tzdata for these zones. The recorded dates tell them apart: '2026-08-27 16:51:11 +0000' against '2026-08-27 16:51:11 +0000', which are the FIXTURE_COMMITS times at +0000 if the env was dropped and 2026-08-27T16:49:56 at +0000 if the zones are missing.
